type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}]}], "template_override": 1}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le11ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le11ob02re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le11ob02re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "Sally's Suitcase<br>\nThe Great Pyramid on the Giza Plateau in Egypt is one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World. It is the only one to survive to modern times. The pyramid stands 442 feet high. The base is 228 feet round. The pyramid is so large you can actually see it from space!", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le11ob02re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "The ancient Egyptians constructed the great pyramid from 2,300,000 blocks. Each block weighed an average of two and a half tons. Workers covered the outside with polished white limestone. It was shiny from a distance. The capstone, or top stone, was plated with gold or silver to flash in the sun.", "id": 2, "time": "25500", "image": "engenn5le11ob02re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Inside, workers built the Queen's and  King's Chambers.  This is where priests entombed the great pharaoh Khufut (koo- foo)  in his sarcophagus. Until the 1400s, this was the tallest monument ever built.", "id": 3, "time": "49500", "image": "engenn5le11ob02re2img01.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Accident-Prone in Egypt"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Wonder of the World"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe rooms, homes and objects in buildings in common social and work situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le11ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Present Simple Tense versus The Past Simple Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that happened in the place and the people who lived there.<br><br>When you are at a historical or ancient site, you use the Simple Present tense to talk about your experience in the present. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The Simple Present Tense \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The Simple Past Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is the only one to <span class=\\\"underline\\\">survive</span> to modern times.  <br><br>  The pyramid <span class=\\\"underline\\\">stands</span> 442 feet high. <br><br>  The base <span class=\\\"underline\\\">is</span> 228 feet around\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The Ancient Egyptians <span class=\\\"underline\\\">constructed</span> the great pyramid from 2,300,000 blocks.<br><br>  Each block <span class=\\\"underline\\\">weighed</span> an average of two and a half tons. <br><br> Until the 1400s, this <span class=\\\"underline\\\">was</span> the tallest monument ever built\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to survive "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to continue; be there after many years "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The pyramids at Giza were the old wonder of the ancient world to survive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about the Great Pyramid."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "modern times"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to live in the present day and age  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am glad I was born in modern times."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "space "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the region outside the atmosphere in which the stars and other planets are situated"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: They travelled through outer space to get to the moon."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to weigh"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to measure how heavy an object is "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I stepped on the scale to weigh myself."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to plate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cover with a thin layer of a different material"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The chain around my neck is gold plated."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to entomb"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to place a body in a vault "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They entombed the king in a the pyramid."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shiny"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is bright because it reflects light "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The gold chain was shiny and new."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sarcophagus"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a stone coffin, used in ancient times "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The body of the king was wrapped and placed in the sarcophagus. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob02aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look up an ancient building online (not the pyramids)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a paragraph  6 - 10 sentences long."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write about the structure and building materials."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write about the size and how people used it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read it to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to your partner's paragraph."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look up an ancient building."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about the structure and materials."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say how people used the building."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my paragraph aloud."}]}], "type": "sena"}